# Design lock

Do not change how the site looks unless the user explicitly asks for a visual change.

Locked: colors, fonts, spacing, radii, shadows, layout, motion, copy placement, Mike artwork, and component visuals.

- Edit `src/styles/global.css` tokens and `@theme` only when asked to restyle
- Never restyle, crop, or redraw files in `src/assets/`
- Structure, refactors, routes, and data moves must keep the same classes, inline styles, and Framer Motion values
- Bug fixes may restore *intended* behavior (e.g. a broken hover class) but must not introduce a new look
- New pages/features must reuse existing tokens (`paper`, `ink`, `cream`, `brandRed`, `brandPurple`, `line`, `card`) and existing section/card patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — unsolicited restyle
<button className="rounded-md bg-black px-3 py-1">Send</button>

// ✅ GOOD — keep the existing pill pattern
<button className="self-start inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full font-semibold text-sm bg-ink text-paper">
  Send
</button>
```
